      "content": "but it's not just a \"mistake\" though. it feels too specific. the way the air felt, the exact sound of the wood in the cabin... it's more real than the records. and i found this old clipping from a biotech firm called NexaGen that was doing \"neurological optimization\" studies in my hometown around that same time. it feels like more than a coincidence. if the records are wrong, how can i trust any of the other documents from that period? can you help me look into NexaGen's history and see if they had anything to do with memory-related research back then?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
